<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Peter Zenger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1697">1697</a>–<a href="/years/1746">1746</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Peter Zenger was a German-born printer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> City whose New-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york-maine">York</a> Weekly Journal attacked Governor William Cosby. Arrested for seditious libel, he was acquitted by a jury in 1735 after his lawyer Andrew Hamilton argued that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> the truth could not be libel. The case became a landmark in the history of press freedom in America.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-peter-zenger.jpg" alt="John Peter Zenger" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: [Andrew Hamilton defending John Peter Zenger in court, 1734-1735, unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Peter_Zenger_trial.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
